#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100608 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100816 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41b7d83f-3b9b-556c-9e49-13df9c3b597e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing the Natural Logarithm"}] :question/id #uuid "8ea17e06-1248-510c-9e71-c57da0cb0d02" :question/math-academy-id "e-14405" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int \\dfrac{3}{x \\sqrt{\\ln x}} \\, \\textrm{d}x }.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u = \\ln x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}u=\\dfrac 1 x\\,{\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2{u}^{1/2}+C \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{u}+C \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100609 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100817 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa28f5c4-135e-576a-baa0-68c41b5139f6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing Other Logarithms"}] :question/id #uuid "1579f932-6e7f-5daa-b001-54a9f6c236ad" :question/math-academy-id "e-14406" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\log^2_3 x }{x} \\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{(\\log_3 x)^2 }{x} \\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=\\log_3 x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{1}{x\\ln 3}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\ln 3\\,\\textrm d u = \\dfrac 1 x \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\int {u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3({log}_{3}⁡x)^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{log}_{3}^{3}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100610 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100818 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a7aff6-d1b2-5383-bb26-aa6363594b05" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Definite Integrals"}] :question/id #uuid "d2f49acf-ed91-510d-a0f1-41c50eeef9e7" :question/math-academy-id "e-14422" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle{\\int_{e}^{e^2} \\dfrac{\\ln^2 x}{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u = \\ln x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}u=\\dfrac 1 x\\,{\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e$ | $e^2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\int_{e}^{e^2} \\dfrac{\\ln^2 x}{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x\n&= \\int_{e}^{e^2} (\\ln x)^2\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{x}\\[5pt]\n&=\\int_{1}^{2} u^2\\,\\textrm{d}u\\[5pt]\n&=\\left.\\dfrac13u^{3}\\right|_{1}^{2}\\[5pt] \n&=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(2^3-1^3 \\right)\\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(8-1 \\right)\\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac{7}{3}\t\t\n\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269163 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100816 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41b7d83f-3b9b-556c-9e49-13df9c3b597e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing the Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1254fcec-98e0-5f67-a76b-6f8a8e44308a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266302} {:answer/id #uuid "2df7ae72-0cf7-5370-8c96-6a976c483816" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266551} {:answer/id #uuid "94c0889d-4b4f-5d2e-afac-f8d8f354ffd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{ln}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267474} {:answer/id #uuid "ad4b89d4-801b-51a5-9299-c541da6954c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267708} {:answer/id #uuid "ee9364d1-6361-5047-8594-cb93beae9749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee9364d1-6361-5047-8594-cb93beae9749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268265} :answer-field/id #uuid "c87b8c31-bac0-55a7-9f5f-8efffda69a26" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268767}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b8d94a83-3a6d-514a-949b-8d2d5e661234" :question/math-academy-id "q-13803" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{u}^{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269169 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100816 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41b7d83f-3b9b-556c-9e49-13df9c3b597e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing the Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "028b5d24-5343-5712-ab0f-d2940e077210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266165} {:answer/id #uuid "2296eb71-af04-5c41-943c-a5d4e6ebc126" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}{ln}^{2}⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266454} {:answer/id #uuid "238496c5-76bc-51bf-9369-36c9de851713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266471} {:answer/id #uuid "47641199-4887-5f5e-986c-9437b93c2232" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266781} {:answer/id #uuid "92224e92-8249-52e3-bd3f-d168ab26bf3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "238496c5-76bc-51bf-9369-36c9de851713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266471} :answer-field/id #uuid "89bcc82a-73ac-56e2-ab50-09b7c5de2e1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268651}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6641fae0-7624-5b24-b01b-edaaed427bd0" :question/math-academy-id "q-13807" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot 2x=\\frac{2}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}\\cdot  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{u}^{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269173 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100816 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41b7d83f-3b9b-556c-9e49-13df9c3b597e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing the Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d002c74-ff20-553d-9136-17296c2d8d2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266826} {:answer/id #uuid "8c5bd3ce-72c6-51a5-95b4-0077a28233d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267398} {:answer/id #uuid "ba510d31-6337-529f-b283-89a45c84c928" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267817} {:answer/id #uuid "bafa205e-e8d6-525e-bbe0-a6d46a971887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267822} {:answer/id #uuid "e9d0db79-ae5a-53ee-b446-50fcd6c6f54f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bafa205e-e8d6-525e-bbe0-a6d46a971887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267822} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e5a6b2e-ccb8-5317-92db-43476ba1348a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268486}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "78bb1805-2714-583b-b597-4f74cc851968" :question/math-academy-id "q-13808" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{5}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot 2x=\\frac{2}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =5\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441899 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100816 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41b7d83f-3b9b-556c-9e49-13df9c3b597e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing the Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cdc4e41-1390-58a2-bac1-3d5ad6ed32e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441875} {:answer/id #uuid "383da31d-fae5-528c-b771-c06390c58c47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441877} {:answer/id #uuid "9a132687-cf9b-5e12-8918-cb54c98b6670" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441886} {:answer/id #uuid "d129af00-45fd-56b1-bfbc-bbc2b9c9a339" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441889} {:answer/id #uuid "e2371163-1bcf-5101-ab68-2260fe787c84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d129af00-45fd-56b1-bfbc-bbc2b9c9a339" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441889} :answer-field/id #uuid "edd22d9f-f6c6-5c79-8b35-f5d0306c51e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cc39d04c-8fc6-5458-bd77-d57b514616c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-13822" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{1}{3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3x}\\cdot 3=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441900 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100818 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a7aff6-d1b2-5383-bb26-aa6363594b05" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Definite Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4403caea-cd74-51a9-b79d-725521c1723f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441878} {:answer/id #uuid "53d5b4d4-65c5-534f-b5bf-9a4d54b10bf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441880} {:answer/id #uuid "74dd2751-1a10-5b13-a07e-4a1b5ceee5f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441882} {:answer/id #uuid "d0c5c72a-52a6-527f-9089-d3942f82a598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441888} {:answer/id #uuid "fa48eb2e-b23d-5975-8ee4-2650534bd1bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441894}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0c5c72a-52a6-527f-9089-d3942f82a598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441888} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e5e2b78-7327-5ca0-90fb-487bdfff6019" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d724ae77-2273-56ab-852e-2415e473e7f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-13840" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{2}}\\frac{2}{5x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot 2x=\\frac{2}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e$ | ${e}^{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{2}}\\frac{2}{5x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{2}}\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{2}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡{2}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441898 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100816 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41b7d83f-3b9b-556c-9e49-13df9c3b597e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing the Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51f5ec9c-cf1f-5d72-a5d8-f8dc65eacd30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441879} {:answer/id #uuid "83e83f58-9225-53a6-8e6a-f42f69406481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441884} {:answer/id #uuid "be58a7fb-a086-5860-ad30-dd1c817fbd59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441887} {:answer/id #uuid "dac76dc6-a248-5bf4-bc16-bc99e472f0d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441890} {:answer/id #uuid "eb90fc15-7950-575d-a8ff-31fa8bd25ec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dac76dc6-a248-5bf4-bc16-bc99e472f0d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441890} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0f12e38-1619-5468-ac12-872947123f4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441896}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "814f2ed7-2079-5a15-870f-7b1832892ba3" :question/math-academy-id "q-210748" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot 2x=\\frac{2}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\sqrt{3}\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{u} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384656 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100817 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa28f5c4-135e-576a-baa0-68c41b5139f6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing Other Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "126fc08e-95cb-5306-9924-3f019148d8ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{log}_{5}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384658} {:answer/id #uuid "c5ca6758-4100-5c28-a5e2-8d3c88248263" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})}{12}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384659} {:answer/id #uuid "8ace6c23-79dc-5742-bc86-816d99045d4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5{log}_{5}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})}{12}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384660} {:answer/id #uuid "c0fb5889-b60d-5aaf-8beb-363ab1698930" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384661} {:answer/id #uuid "4cc9eae9-b3ce-547a-9a34-0e08774a75ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ace6c23-79dc-5742-bc86-816d99045d4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5{log}_{5}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})}{12}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384660} :answer-field/id #uuid "c996e19a-d711-54dc-9b49-a03cea7cecd2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384657}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6517d214-0493-5c34-bfbe-5920e35412fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-210751" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{{log}_{5}⁡({x}^{3})}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={log}_{5}⁡({x}^{3}).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{3}\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{5}⁡({x}^{3})}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int {log}_{5}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int u\\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{3}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{6}\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{6}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5{log}_{5}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})}{12}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290281 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100817 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa28f5c4-135e-576a-baa0-68c41b5139f6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing Other Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3783aaf0-95fe-582e-9b6c-214d1b88d33f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{3}⁡(2x)|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288408} {:answer/id #uuid "37ab6ab5-1c0e-58f5-b386-e76cdaa7443e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{3}⁡(2x)|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288410} {:answer/id #uuid "4d666098-aa58-56fe-865c-a47cdc80ed88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{3}⁡(2x)|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288570} {:answer/id #uuid "be835456-2ece-556e-a15f-dfc8e8723b39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3|{log}_{3}⁡(2x)|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289286} {:answer/id #uuid "efd7546d-984c-5ba3-b883-fe67852b9b22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289618}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37ab6ab5-1c0e-58f5-b386-e76cdaa7443e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{3}⁡(2x)|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288410} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a19bf0f-f7af-52cd-8c16-c823fa1c1794" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "550df46c-f0bc-5517-a411-d24ef095d3fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-210781" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{3}{x{log}_{3}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={log}_{3}⁡(2x).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{x{log}_{3}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{{log}_{3}⁡(2x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{3}{u}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{3}⁡(2x)|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101371 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100817 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa28f5c4-135e-576a-baa0-68c41b5139f6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing Other Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "097bf9be-35d0-5117-aeeb-185f65a4e444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295316} {:answer/id #uuid "0c595f3e-4a64-5335-bfee-ef4f9c199d44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295335} {:answer/id #uuid "3a9d8072-eeac-5190-ac53-423bbc5c0d15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295602} {:answer/id #uuid "7c854fd3-91d0-5ade-bfec-4aa656855a88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}^{2}⁡x}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295948} {:answer/id #uuid "943f1ef0-98c7-561c-8c98-1ab90aa0f4c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "943f1ef0-98c7-561c-8c98-1ab90aa0f4c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296059} :answer-field/id #uuid "94521d82-e55e-520c-aa39-65e9dae6d07e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296944}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bc1950d7-cc9c-5e9a-8f86-5dcc05de2e91" :question/math-academy-id "q-31329" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={log}_{2}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {log}_{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297379 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100817 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa28f5c4-135e-576a-baa0-68c41b5139f6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing Other Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a00bd77-f937-55b8-9148-a5c1a2df5750" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{3}⁡x}{2}+C" :db/id #ed